From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 19:41:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: a733: Take the MBUS clock from PLL_PERI0

MBUS_CLK_REG selects 600 MHz, 480 MHz and 400 MHz with the values 001,
011 and 100. The A733 manual names these sources PERI0_600M, PERI0_480M
and PERI0_400M, and its clock tree lists MBUS under PLL_PERI0. The
driver maps them to the PLL_PERI1 outputs, so the clock tree shows mbus
and every mbus gate under pll-periph1-600M while the value the firmware
sets selects PLL_PERI0, and a rate change on PLL_PERI1 would be reported
as a change of mbus.

Map the three values to the PLL_PERI0 outputs. The register is not
written: the value the firmware set stays, only the parent Linux sees
for it changes.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted to a shell; with the PERI1 2x output
gated, a read from the SD card through MBUS completed with the same data
while a clock on PERI1_600M stood still.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
index 1df3f76fced9..ee5925122e0e 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
@@ -533,10 +533,10 @@ static SUNXI_CCU_GATE_DATA(bus_its_pcie0_aclk_clk, "bus-its-pcie0-aclk", hosc, 0
 
 static const struct clk_parent_data mbus_parents[] = {
 	{ .hw = &sys_24M_clk.hw },
-	{ .hw = &pll_periph1_600M_clk.hw },
+	{ .hw = &pll_periph0_600M_clk.hw },
 	{ .hw = &pll_ddr_clk.common.hw },
-	{ .hw = &pll_periph1_480M_clk.common.hw },
-	{ .hw = &pll_periph1_400M_clk.hw },
+	{ .hw = &pll_periph0_480M_clk.common.hw },
+	{ .hw = &pll_periph0_400M_clk.hw },
 	{ .hw = &pll_npu_clk.common.hw },
 };
 static SUNXI_CCU_M_DATA_WITH_MUX_GATE_FEAT(mbus_clk, "mbus", mbus_parents, 0x588,
